00:57:00,000 --> 00:57:06,000
Stomp the Yard is a 2007 American dance drama film  produced by Rainforest Films and
released through Sony Pictures' Screen Gems division on January 12, 2007.

12
01:02:10,909 --> 01:02:16,909
Directed by Sylvain White, Stomp the Yard centers on DJ Williams, a college student at a fictional
historically black university who pledges to join a fictional Greek-letter fraternity.

13
01:07:21,818 --> 01:07:27,818
The film's central conflict involves DJ's fraternity competing in various
stepping competitions against a rival fraternity of the same school.

14
01:12:32,727 --> 01:12:38,727
The film's script was written by Robert Adetuyi, working from
an original draft by Gregory Ramon Anderson.

15
01:17:43,636 --> 01:17:49,636
The film was originally titled Steppin', but to avoid confusion
over the 2006 film Step Up, the title was changed.

16
01:22:54,545 --> 01:23:00,545
Delta Sigma Theta along with other sororities
like Gamma Theta were in the movie.

17
01:28:05,454 --> 01:28:11,454
The film stars Columbus Short, Meagan Good, Darrin Henson, Brian White, Laz Alonso, and Valarie
Pettiford, with Harry Lennix, and, in their film debuts, R&B singers Ne-Yo & Chris Brown.

18
01:33:16,363 --> 01:33:22,363
Stomp the Yard was filmed in Atlanta, Georgia, on the campuses of Morris Brown College, Georgia Institute of Technology,
Morehouse College, and Clark Atlanta University, and in the MAK Historic District of Decatur, Georgia.

19
01:38:27,272 --> 01:38:33,272
Elsewhere Short, Alonso and Brown had also starred
together in the film This Christmas.

20
01:43:38,181 --> 01:43:44,181
The film explores themes of daughter, loss of loved
one, love at first sight, breakdance.

21
